    "current_example": {
      "math_academy_id": "e-974",
      "problem": "Plot the point $C$ with coordinates $(1,-2)$ on the Cartesian plane.",
      "worked_solution": "Starting at the origin $O,$ we move along the $x$ and $y$ axes to get to the point $C.$\n\nFirst, we move along the $x$-axis. The point $C$ has an $x$-coordinate of $1,$ so we move $1$ unit to the *right*, in the *positive* direction of the $x$-axis.\n\nThen, we move along the $y$-axis. The point $C$ has a $y$-coordinate of $-2,$ so we move $2$ units *down*, in the *negative* direction of the $y$-axis.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14129504/assets/49069b4b9be29c0a999e7d2b71eec9a973eda9ad1f8a2a7b897d76970771a644.png)",
